    {
      "id": "cymbeline/sceneIV_7.3/p@156736",
      "type": "passage",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "A fever with the absence of her son;\nA madness, of which her life’s in danger. Heavens,\nHow deeply you at once do touch me! Imogen,\nThe great part of my comfort, gone; my queen\nUpon a desperate bed, and in a time\nWhen fearful wars point at me; her son gone,\nSo needful for this present. It strikes me past\nThe hope of comfort. But for thee, fellow,\nWho needs must know of her departure and\nDost seem so ignorant, we’ll enforce it from thee\nBy a sharp torture.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
